        "description": {
          "type": "/type/text",
          "value": "\"Winner of the Pulitzer Prize and the American Book Award, The Soul of a New Machine was a bestseller on its first publication in 1981. With the touch of an expert thriller writer, Tracy Kidder recounts the feverish efforts of a team of Data General researchers to create a new 32-bit superminicomputer. A compelling account of individual sacrifice and human ingenuity, The Soul of a New Machine endures as the classic chronicle of the computer age and the masterminds behind its technological advances.\".\n\n\"Tracy Kidder has written a new Introduction to this Modern Library edition.\"--BOOK JACKET."
        },
